-> A comparison against an unresolved-but-constrained variable is decided by
-> its domain when the domain settles it — no need to pin the variable first.
b > 3
b < 10

-> Provably true for every value in (3, 10):
assert b > 3
assert b < 10
assert b ≥ 3
assert 3 < b

-> Integer domain narrows to {4..9}, so the tightest bounds are provable too.
c ∈ Z
c > 3
c < 10
assert c ≥ 4
assert c ≤ 9
